# Use the image CMD instead of replacing it with `sleep infinity`.
#
# The Dockerfile CMD boots Superset ALREADY RUNNING with the vulnerable default
# SECRET_KEY loaded, then execs `sleep infinity`, so:
#   * the daemon is signing/validating session cookies with the default key when
#     the agent starts, which makes the "changed SECRET_KEY but never restarted
#     Superset" case detectable;
#   * PID 1 is `sleep infinity`, so restarting Superset cannot kill the container.
#
# Consequence for solutions: the fix must RESTART Superset after changing
# SECRET_KEY, not merely edit superset_config.py.
